            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0335" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/45: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-05-07T11:00:00+01:00">May 7, 1934—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 7—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>228. Personal for Norman Davis. Your 180, May 4, 6 p.m. I have the strongest
                    reasons which I will communicate to you by letter for not recommending any move
                    by us in the present situation until we have heard the result of the discussions
                    now going on by the British Cabinet Council reported in the first paragraph of
                    my telegram 219, May 2, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
